[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Keep workspace generations monotonic across a daemon restart

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @repo

[WORK]
UID: WORK-SCRIBE-GENERATION-ACROSS-RESTART
TITLE: Keep workspace generations monotonic across a daemon restart
DEPTH: sketch
AUTHORED_BY: llm
STATEMENT: >>>
The workspace generation counter is monotonic within one daemon process only
(scribe_workspace.py, _last_generation_number). A scribe restart resets it, so
a long-lived board process that cached generation N can take a false cache hit
after the daemon comes back with the same number for different content. Make
the number survive a restart (persist it beside the socket, or derive it from
content: a hash of the loaded corpus) or make the board key its cache on
something the daemon cannot repeat.
<<<
NOTES: >>>
Found by the dry-run re-review on 2026-09-04 after the in-process fix landed in
ede251ef; the within-process contract (test_rpc_dry_run_generation) does not
cover a restart.
<<<
